abstract: >-
  xfeeds is a self-updating, open threat intelligence pipeline that collects,
  normalizes, enriches, scores, filters, and publishes malicious-IP indicators
  in interoperable formats including CSV, JSON, STIX 2.1, MISP, and firewall
  rule sets. Unlike naive aggregation of public blocklists, which manufactures
  false confidence because many public lists mirror or re-derive one another,
  xfeeds models source dependency explicitly. Sources are assigned independence
  classes and only the strongest contribution within a class counts toward
  corroboration, while freshness gating prevents dormant observations from
  independently promoting an indicator. Redistribution rights are enforced
  structurally: restricted sources may raise confidence without appearing in
  published records, and separate non-commercial and clean-provenance feed
  tiers carry distinct redistribution promises.
keywords:
  - threat intelligence
  - indicators of compromise
